{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And the men are shepherds of sheep, for they were men of cattle.</b> One must examine why it was necessary to give a reason for his words, 'for they were men of cattle' — whether they were men of cattle or not, after all they are shepherds of sheep. And further, for he said (Genesis 46:33), 'For when Pharaoh will call you and say, What is your occupation, you shall say, Men of cattle were your servants' — it would have been more fitting for them to say, 'Shepherds of sheep were your servants,' for it is specifically shepherds of sheep who are an abomination to the Egyptians, but not men of cattle — and did Pharaoh not have cattle? And another difficulty: that they changed and did not say as Joseph had commanded them, for they answered Pharaoh (Genesis 47:3), 'Shepherds of sheep were your servants.' And further, 'also our fathers' is superfluous — did he ask them about the doings of their fathers?'" "And the explanation of the matter is that the purpose of all these things was so that Pharaoh would distance them from himself and settle them in the land of Goshen. Even though Pharaoh too had sheep and cattle and shepherds, nevertheless the shepherds of Egypt were accustomed to treat the species of sheep with honor, on account of the sign of Aries, in which they placed their trust — and the honor would be to graze them in a fat and good pasture, a broad meadow, and not to strike them with rods; but other nations are not careful about this. Therefore an abomination to the Egyptians was every shepherd of sheep. Consequently, when Joseph said to Pharaoh, 'And the men are shepherds of sheep,' in order to distance them from himself, he needed to give a reason of exoneration, so that they would not be suspected that they chose the trade of shepherding in order to blunt the teeth of all those who believe in the sign of Aries, when they see the sheep passing under the staff, struck and afflicted. Therefore he gave the reason, 'for they were men of cattle' — that this is what happened to them, that the principal part of their property was cattle; therefore they chose for themselves the trade of shepherding."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:44.984470659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}